    <briefdescription>
<para>This server-only header derives the XilSecure library capability bitmap at compile time. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Each build-gated feature contributes one permanently-assigned bit (see XSecure_LibCapBit in <ref refid="xsecure__defs_8h" kindref="compound">xsecure_defs.h</ref>) to the aggregate XSECURE_LIB_CAPABILITIES constant, which the Features command reports to the client alongside the library version.</para><para>It lives in server/core (shared server code) rather than a per-platform directory so a single derivation is reused across platforms: the gate macros are named consistently, and a feature not compiled into a given platform simply leaves its gate undefined and contributes 0.</para><para>Derivation is entirely compile time (a chain of ifdef checks OR&apos;d together), so there is no runtime cost: a feature that is not compiled in simply contributes 0. Bits are append-only - a new capability consumes a new, previously-zero bit and never disturbs existing assignments, so older clients stay compatible.</para><para>Feature gating:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>PLM_SECURE_EXCLUDE is the umbrella switch: when defined, the whole secure crypto set (RSA + ECDSA + AES) is excluded, so all of those bits read 0.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Inside it, PLM_RSA_EXCLUDE and PLM_ECDSA_EXCLUDE are the finer per-engine gates. AES has no finer gate, so AES presence == !PLM_SECURE_EXCLUDE.</para></listitem><listitem><para>ECC curve support macros: P-192/P-224/P-256/P-521 are BSP configurable (xsecure_config.h for SDT, xparameters.h for the classic flow); P-384 is always supported when ECDSA is in the build.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XSECURE_CRYPTOALGINFO_ENABLED is independent of the secure engines.</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para><para><preformatted>
MODIFICATION HISTORY:</preformatted></para><para><preformatted>Ver   Who  Date        Changes
<hruler/>

5.8   tus  08/21/26    Initial release with ECDSA/RSA/AES/crypto-alg-info and
                       ECC big-endian capability bits</preformatted></para><para><preformatted></preformatted> </para>    </detaileddescription>
